      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:5:9",
      "text": [
        " أَهْلِهِ حَتَّى يَرْدَعَ عَلَى جَسَدِهِ ",
        "وَ قَالَ قَالَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) كُنَّا نَلْبَسُ الْمُعَصْفَرَ فِي الْبَيْتِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Ja’far Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Al Qaddah, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> that Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> had a sheet made in Wars (a city), wearing it among his<sup>saww</sup> family until he<sup>asws</sup> turned it upon his<sup>saww</sup> body’. ",
          "And he (the narrator) said, ‘Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘We<sup>asws</sup> wear the dyed clothes in the house’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "9. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from Ja‘far ibn Muhammad from ibn al-Qaddah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause, had a sheet that was from Wars (a place in Yemen). He (the Messenger of Allah) would use it in the family. The color of the sheet had left marks on him (the Messenger of Allah).’ Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘We would use al-Mu‘asfar (dye with safflower) clothes at home.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
